# ⭐ SECTION 3 — RELATIONSHIPS (Ultra‑Detailed)

### Breakdown ↔ Technician  
- Breakdown.technicianId → Unit.unitId (type: technician)

### Breakdown ↔ Driver  
- Breakdown.driverId → Unit.unitId (type: driver)

### Breakdown ↔ GPS  
- GPS.unitId → Breakdown.unitId

### Breakdown ↔ ProtocolHistory  
- ProtocolHistory.breakdownId → Breakdown.id

### Breakdown ↔ Logs  
- Log.breakdownId → Breakdown.id

### Vendor ↔ Region  
- Vendor.region → Breakdown.location region (future)

---

# ⭐ SECTION 4 — INDEXING STRATEGY

### High‑priority indexes:

```javascript
BreakdownSchema.index({ unitId: 1 });
BreakdownSchema.index({ status: 1 });

GPSSchema.index({ unitId: 1, timestamp: -1 });

UnitSchema.index({ type: 1 });
UnitSchema.index({ status: 1 });

ProtocolHistorySchema.index({ breakdownId: 1 });
```

These indexes give:

- Fast GPS lookups  
- Fast breakdown filtering  
- Fast technician assignment  
- Fast emergency protocol retrieval  

---

# ⭐ SECTION 5 — VALIDATION RULES

### Breakdown Validation
- Must have unitId  
- Must have driverId  
- Must have valid status  
- Must enforce repair‑only repairPath  

### GPS Validation
- Must have lat/lon  
- Must have timestamp  
- Must have valid unit type  

### Vendor Validation
- Must be repair‑only  
- Must not include tow services  

---

# ⭐ SECTION 6 — NO‑TOW ENFORCEMENT IN DATABASE

### Vendors
- `type: "repair"` only  
- No tow vendors allowed  

### Units
- No unit type “tow truck” allowed  

### Logs
- No tow‑related steps allowed  

### ProtocolHistory
- No tow‑related metadata allowed  

---

# ⭐ SECTION 7 — Grace Engine Integration Points

Grace uses:

- Breakdown.severity  
- Breakdown.repairPath  
- GPS.latest  
- Unit.status  
- Vendor.repairOnly  
- ProtocolHistory.steps  
- Logs  

This gives Grace full intelligence to execute:

- Emergency protocol  
- Technician dispatch  
- Routing  
- Vendor selection  
- After‑hours workflows  

